  "semantic_fragments": [
    {
      "fragment_type": "working_principle",
      "content": "This product is a high-tech infra-red (IR) thermometer designed to take human body temperature by measuring the energy of IR emitted from the forehead. The product will help you to assess you and your family members' health conditions easily and quickly.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "infrared thermometer",
        "forehead temperature",
        "IR energy",
        "body temperature measurement"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Infrared Forehead Thermometer",
        "Risk Assessment Report"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "scope_limitation",
      "content": "The risk management activity including the risk management plan was began at the time the project is approved. This risk management review is to assess the harm and make the risk analysis, evaluation, and proposed the risk control plan.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk management",
        "risk analysis",
        "risk evaluation",
        "risk control plan"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Risk Management Plan",
        "PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "Criteria for risk evaluation: Please find the document Risk Management Plan (PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0) for the risk acceptance criteria. Severity scale: 1 Negligible; 2 Minor; 3 Serious; 4 Critical; 5 Catastrophic. Probability scale: 1 Few; 2 Improbable; 3 Remote; 4 Occasional; 5 Probable; 6 Frequent.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk acceptance criteria",
        "severity",
        "probability",
        "risk evaluation"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Risk Management Plan",
        "PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "scope_limitation",
      "content": "Document structure covers: Signification of Abbreviations, Overview (product introduction, risk management plan implementation, risk management group), Criteria for risk evaluation, Identify medical device characteristics that could impact on safety and intended use (bibliography, questions from Annex A of ISO/TR 24971:2020, questions from IEC 60601-1:2005+AMD1:2012+AMD2:2020 Edition 3.2, additional questions from IEC 60601-1-2:2014+A1:2020 edition 4.1), Risk analysis/risk evaluation and PRM, Risk Management Conclusion, Signature of the risk management group.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "document structure",
        "ISO/TR 24971:2020",
        "IEC 60601-1",
        "IEC 60601-1-2",
        "risk management"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Risk Assessment Report",
        "Infrared Forehead Thermometer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "For each unacceptable Risk, we have considered risk control measures according to the principle of section3.3 'Risk Acceptance Criteria' in RMP. For each acceptable risk, we have further implemented risk control measures. So I think we have reduced the risk AFAP.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk acceptance",
        "ALARP",
        "AFAP",
        "risk control",
        "RMP"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Risk Management Plan",
        "Risk Acceptance Criteria"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Wireless coexistence (R56): The APP provides display and storage functions. If the app cannot receive the result, the LED of IFT can display the result. When the interference disappears, the next Bluetooth transmission can upload the data lost last time. Therefore, even if the app cannot display the current results, or the app delays the display of the current results, it will not cause harm to the user, but will increase the user's inconvenience.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "wireless coexistence",
        "Bluetooth",
        "LED fallback",
        "data recovery",
        "app display"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "R56",
        "software design",
        "Bluetooth transmission"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Risk Management Conclusion: According to the risk acceptance table, the risk levels before control are distributed as follows. Probability level 6 Frequent / Severity 3 Serious: R50. Probability level 4 Occasional / Severity 2 Minor: R36. Probability level 4 Occasional / Severity 3 Serious: R9, R10, R11, R13, R15, R16, R17, R18, R20, R21, R22, R26, R27, R28, R29, R30, R33, R34, R37, R39, R40, R42, R43, R44, R46, R51, R52, R53. Probability level 3 Remote / Severity 1 Negligible: R56. Probability level 3 Remote / Severity 2 Minor: R23. Probability level 3 Remote / Severity 3 Serious: R24, R38, R54, R55, R57. Probability level 3 Remote / Severity 4 Critical: R3, R8. Probability level 2 Improbable / Severity 3 Serious: R12, R19, R25, R31, R32, R35, R41, R45, R47, R48, R49. Probability level 2 Improbable / Severity 4 Critical: R1, R2, R4, R5, R6, R7, R14. Risks in the White background area are ACC (acceptable); others require control measures. Based on the above risk analysis and assessment, the software security level is determined as B.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk acceptance",
        "risk matrix",
        "risk level",
